  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, but I couldn't confirm it compiles or renders. `node_modules/@aura3d/` is empty in this sandbox, so `typecheck` reports only \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\". With the module unresolved, TypeScript treats every engine call as `any` and checks none of them. I wrote the code against the signatures in `docs/agents/api-signatures.md` and the recipe sources, and I never saw it draw.\n\nWhat it builds:\n- **Body:** a red ellipsoid, with a black glass cabin dome and a red roof panel on top, plus four dark rubber wheels with chrome hubs.\n- **Paint:** `material.physical` with metallic 0.55, clearcoat 1 and clearcoat roughness 0.03. About 1100 tiny metallic flakes sit just above the body surface as an instanced layer (five red/peach colours), which is my own approach to the flake sparkle, since I found no flake option in the docs.\n- **Trim:** a chrome belt line made of 220 small spheres, chrome headlights and bumpers, and red emissive tail lights.\n- **Turntable:** a glossy dark circular platform with chrome studs, so the rotation is visible, and an emissive ring light under the lip. The group `turntable` rotates at 20°/s and the camera stays still, low and front-three-quarter.\n- **Lighting:** `environments.studio`, three long `lights.softbox` strips (left, right, overhead), a shadowed key light, a faint blue rim light and a light bloom, on a near-black background.\n- **State and ready flag:** `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { turntableAngleDeg, paintFinish: 'clearcoat' }` is updated every frame. The angle comes from elapsed time, so it keeps increasing. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nNot confirmed, and worth checking in a real browser:\n- **Soft-box reflections:** the strips' reflections on the paint depend on what the `studio` environment preset provides.\n- **Floor mirror:** I did not add a mirrored copy of the car, so the floor reflects only the environment.\n- **Light brightness:** I could not calibrate the light ",
